  "facts": [
    {
      "id": "daemon-surfaces",
      "claim": "Each companion-daemon provider type now declares the surfaces the daemon serves for it: Codex receives Responses requests as sent instead of over the Chat fallback, the setup-token Anthropic provider answers non-streaming Messages natively, Copilot, Antigravity and anonymous OpenCode Zen list Chat Completions alone, and a surface a type lacks is refused before anything is sent.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/providers/extension_vertical.go; go/internal/providers/extension_vertical_test.go; go/internal/router/extension_failover_test.go"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "rate-limit",
      "claim": "LLMGW_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE limits the /v1 requests one caller starts in a UTC minute on the process and refuses the rest with 429 and Retry-After; a key or project quota refusal carries Retry-After until the refusing window ends.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/api/rate_limit.go; go/internal/api/keypolicy.go; go/internal/iam/quota.go"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "observability",
      "claim": "LLMGW_ACCESS_LOG=json writes one JSON line per request to standard output; GET /metrics serves Prometheus text to a bearer of LLMGW_METRICS_TOKEN and answers 404 when the variable is unset; the request log reads X-LLMGW-Adapted from the response.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/api/observe.go; go/internal/api/metrics.go; go/internal/api/server.go; go/internal/api/logging.go"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "admin-listings",
      "claim": "GET /admin/api/requests lists recorded requests with filters and before_id paging; GET /admin/api/audit takes filters and before_id and returns next_before_id; the usage report's breakdown applies the report's time range and filters.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/api/admin.go; go/internal/api/audit.go; go/internal/iam/usage_events.go; go/internal/iam/audit.go; go/internal/iam/usage.go"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "console",
      "claim": "The console adds Requests and Audit log pages for administrators, charts usage by a chosen metric with a breakdown table, and its committed bundle is rebuilt. The CLI-collected changed paths stop at the renamed stylesheet, so they omit these console paths that git diff --name-status v1.4.1..HEAD lists: dist/assets/index-D224xWlm.js (added), dist/assets/index-DfZps-P8.js (deleted), dist/index.html, src/App.tsx, src/lib/activity.ts (added), src/lib/navigation.ts, src/lib/usage.ts, src/pages/AuditLog.tsx (added), src/pages/Requests.tsx (added), src/pages/Settings.tsx, src/pages/UsageQuotas.tsx, src/styles/base.css, tests/activity.test.mjs (added) and tests/usage-report.test.mjs, all under go/internal/web/console.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "git diff --name-status v1.4.1..HEAD -- go/internal/web/console"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "admin-keys-on-data-plane",
      "claim": "LLMGW_ADMIN_KEYS_ON_DATA_PLANE, true by default, decides whether /v1 accepts the static administrator keys; false refuses them with 403 while /admin/api still accepts them, and the first /v1 request each static key authenticates logs a warning naming its fingerprint.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/api/auth.go; go/internal/config/config.go; go/internal/api/static_key_data_plane_test.go"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "docs-and-examples",
      "claim": "Documentation and the example Compose and environment files describe the new settings, the deprecation of static keys on /v1, the access log and metrics, and link the release notes.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "docs/; README.md; SECURITY.md; deploy/.env.example; deploy/docker-compose.prod.yml; docker-compose.yml"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "error-envelopes",
      "claim": "An unreadable body on POST /v1/chat/completions and /v1/responses gets 422 with the OpenAI envelope of type invalid_request_error, and on POST /v1/messages 422 with the Anthropic envelope whose top-level type is error; these handlers did not change since v1.4.1.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/api/openai.go:237; go/internal/api/responses_api.go:27; go/internal/api/anthropic.go:98; go/internal/api/errors.go:68-119"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "admin-authentication",
      "claim": "Every /admin/api route requires administrator authentication, independent of LLMGW_ALLOW_UNAUTHENTICATED_API, and answers a caller without it with 401 Admin authentication required.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/api/sso.go:92"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "embedded-console",
      "claim": "GET /console/ serves the console index embedded in the binary, whose title is LLM Gateway Console.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/api/server.go:160-162; go/internal/web/console/index.html"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "exploratory-run",
      "claim": "An exploratory run of the draft that became contract da05219969e0 against a binary built from this source, served with LLMGW_ALLOW_UNAUTHENTICATED_API=1 as the release smoke serves it, passed all ten assertions.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "local exploratory run"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verification",
      "claim": "At source revision b22214c299f14ba06482f520ce5b701c0bd5140e: go build, go vet, staticcheck, gofmt, go test for every package, govulncheck, go mod tidy -diff and go mod verify pass; console typecheck, 160 tests, npm audit and the dist rebuild check pass; the documentation check, actionlint, the acceptance-policy tests (18) and the roster script tests pass; go test -race over every package passes on linux/amd64 with Go 1.26.8; the deterministic Docker acceptance passes all 31 checks against an image built from that revision on a Linux engine, where its digest policy does not apply to a locally built candidate.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "local and remote Linux test execution"
      }
    }
  ],
